  "articleBody": "Discovering damaged molding in your home can be a real headache, but knowing the right steps to take can make the repair process smooth and stress-free. First things first, try to figure out what actually caused the damage. Was it an accidental bump, water exposure, or something else entirely? Understanding the cause helps determine the best course of action. Once you know what you're dealing with, you need to assess if the molding can be repaired or if it needs to be completely replaced. Sometimes, a simple patch-up will do, but other times, especially with more intricate designs or structural issues, a modification or replacement might be necessary. When you're ready to get some help, look for a reputable service that starts by really examining the problem, maybe even with photos. They should be able to explain the proposed fix, give you a written proposal with clear costs and lead times, and describe how they'll verify the repair is solid. At HH Remodeling LLC, serving the greater Denver area including Castle Rock and Highlands Ranch, we pride ourselves on transparent communication and quality work. Don't hesitate to reach out for an expert opinion and a reliable solution.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
